{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences","id":1032595,"title":"Imperium Rites, Ascension and it's consequences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T05:26:42-08:00","id":1032595,"title":"Imperium Rites, Ascension and it's consequences","content":"Okay, so here is my question. Let's assume we have Aswadim (for example, Theumiel from Imperial Mysteries), who have accepted Supreme Earthly Omen - to destroy all Earth by flooding in the Abyss. <i>The Pax Arcanum does not apply to Imperium</i>, so technically Exarchs can't just punch him in the face outright without other Ascended Aswadim to retaliate (let's assume they care enough about our Aswadim for some reason). Our Aswadim prepares his Rites, create doomsday cults and prophecies, create his Anti-Messiah, Seals his Omens, then Exalts them and poof! He is Descended and Earth is destroyed.<br /> What happens next? As I understand, destruction of Earth is Supernal Truth on some level now - perfect and unassailable. Do Exarchs re-create world from the scratch? Can they do it without destroying Supernal Truth about destruction of Earth? Is changes brought by Ascension are immutable and perfect, or they are just as any other Supernal Truth - malleable by sufficiently strong power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:39:30-08:00","id":1032600,"title":"","content":"Given the fact that one of the options as far as imperium rites goes includes removing an exarch from power and another being the destruction of the abyss, I'd say that such a thing could be undone...most likely.<br /> <br /> However, you are incorrect in saying the exarchs would be incapable of striking at such an archmage. The exarchs do not have to abide by the pax, nor are they greatly threatened by archmages. It takes a truly herculean effort to strike at the exarchs, whereas they can strike at archmages with comparitive ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:54:19-08:00","id":1032606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032600#post1032600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, you are incorrect in saying the exarchs would be incapable of striking at such an archmage. The exarchs do not have to abide by the pax, nor are they greatly threatened by archmages. It takes a truly herculean effort to strike at the exarchs, whereas they can strike at archmages with comparitive ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not saying that they can't, but not without consequences. Note that I said &quot;Ascended Aswadim to retaliate&quot;, not &quot;Aswadim to retaliate&quot;. Exarchs are most powerful Ascended beings, but not the only ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:41:51-08:00","id":1032654,"title":"","content":"I am reminded of all those high-power, high-stakes mystical/cosmic comics stories where an omnicidal baddie achieves godlike power or manipulates a cosmic entity into destroying the world, and the surviving heroes have to put things back together by defeating them and undoing the damage. I suppose it works pretty much the same thing here. One Aswadim Archmage does apocalyptic damage to the world with an Imperium rite of theirs, an Archmage from another faction undoes the damage with another Imperium rite. And Ochemata from Exarchs or Ascended Pentacle mages may make an emergency intervention. Of course, the repair might not be... flawless, leading to various kinds of changes to the timeline (this happens a lot in comics, too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:27:48-08:00","id":1032711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032654#post1032654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am reminded of all those high-power, high-stakes mystical/cosmic comics stories where an omnicidal baddie achieves godlike power or manipulates a cosmic entity into destroying the world, and the surviving heroes have to put things back together by defeating them and undoing the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is mostly about what happens after omnicidal baddie succeeds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:48:18-08:00","id":1032734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032711#post1032711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is mostly about what happens after omnicidal baddie succeeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically speaking, the change seems shocking enough for the Tellurian at large to have the same apocalyptic effects as the Fall of Atlantis and the Death of Father Wolf, although with the physical world (temporarily) gone, the other Realms would be the ones to bear the brunt of the shock. Think of a vast shockwave arising from the big hole where the physical realm stood and sweeping the Shadow, the Astral, and the Underworld, perhaps even affecting the Abyss, the Supernal, and the Lower Depths to some degree. Even if and when the other Archmages, Supernal beings, and the godlike beings that act as patrons for the other supernatural splats act to repair the damage, bring back the world, and stabilize the universe, this is the kind of cosmic event that is likely to leave permanent changes in the Tellurian, or at least extensive scars that last an entire age, much like the the ruins of the Time Before endured across the world for the entire Neolithic. This is the kind of event that may well justify radical changes happening in the setting, such as say Quiescence, the Gauntlet, and all kinds of Masquerade collapsing and the CoD becoming an Unmasqued World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:09:15-08:00","id":1032747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032734#post1032734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is the kind of cosmic event that is likely to leave permanent changes in the Tellurian</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting part, because it seems that some Ascensions are more likely to permanently affect Tellurian than the others. For example (from now on, these are speculations on material in Imperial Mysteries), Ascension of Hyperion &quot;merely&quot; created the most popular and influential religion ever, and Ascension of Corpus Author seems to have &quot;locked&quot; Mysterium in place, but none of these are as permanent as scale of permanent changes you described.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:20:49-08:00","id":1032753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032747#post1032747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascension of Corpus Author seems to have &quot;locked&quot; Mysterium in place, but none of these are as permanent as scale of permanent changes you described.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must understand that Corpus Author Ascension created Mysterium by showing 'She had right, we must agree on one Order thing', not magically sweeping around the world with every Pancryptias and Keepers of the Word instantly becoming Mysterium now. just most of caucuses of those two Orders agreed that Corpus Author was right, not that they were instant Order swap with spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:49:37-08:00","id":1032768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032753#post1032753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You must understand that Corpus Author Ascension created Mysterium by showing 'She had right, we must agree on one Order thing', not magically sweeping around the world with every Pancryptias and Keepers of the Word instantly becoming Mysterium now. just most of caucuses of those two Orders agreed that Corpus Author was right, not that they were instant Order swap with spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Imperial Rite changes entire history retroactively, I really fail to see the difference. Of course they agreed. Their entire history was written in such way that they agreed on &quot;one Order thing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:53:08-08:00","id":1032773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences#post1032595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... <i>The Pax Arcanum does not apply to Imperium</i>, so technically Exarchs can't just punch him in the face outright without other Ascended Aswadim to retaliate (let's assume they care enough about our Aswadim for some reason). ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The default state is &quot;there are no rules&quot;, and the pax is the exception. So actually, if the pax does not apply, that means everyone can punch him/her in the face outright without triggering the pax. And then, the Exarchs (or any other ascended being) are not covered by the pax, and can punch everyone whenever they like. It seems you mistake the pax arcana as an defense alliance like the NATO, while it is actually more a common understanding in a cold war situation.<br /> <br /> And then finally, you assume ascended aswadim would do anything at all. They ascended and reached their goal of severing all ties to the supernal realms and became the rulers of their own realms /universes. Why would they care about or even notice anything the aswadim archmage does?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But let's assume the aswadim manages to break the fallen world in his quest to ascension. So at some point in time, the fallen world just ends. However, time is a thing that is only linear in the fallen world, as any archmage in the time arcanum would tell you. So it is basically still there, with its expiration date. And any archmage or ascended being can change that again prior to that date. However, the aswadim has basically removed itself from existance again and reached her goal, so it wont matter to her either.<br /> <br /> It would have a much higher impact, if the aswadim would not create some cosmic change herself but instead unmake a change in the past. Then to change that again would be almost as difficult as the original task(there are some left-over pieces scattered around existance). But unmaking the Fall pretty much offends every ascended being (probably even the ascended aswadim, because unmaking the Fall also unmakes the Abyss). If you want to target lower, but still damage the Fallen world in a drastic way, try to unmake te building of a watchtower or the creation of vampires/werewolves/etc.<br /> <br /> Actually, that could be an interesting story hook for any kind of mage story: Find remnants of (or even persons affiliated with) an entirely different watchtower in another supernal realm. One that has been unmade again by other supernal forces in the attempt (or success) of ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3278,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","user":"Tyloron","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","name":"Tyloron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:11:11-08:00","id":1032779,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyloron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032773#post1032773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, the Exarchs (or any other ascended being) are not covered by the pax, and can punch everyone whenever they like.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reason then for Exarchs not to crush Alienated, Examplars and Bodhisattvas ententes completely. Same goes for the other Ascended beings and ententes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyloron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032773#post1032773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems you mistake the pax arcana as an defense alliance like the NATO</div> </div> </div> </div>Ententes <i>are</i> alliances, it's outright stated so in their descriptions. Defense is one thing alliances built for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyloron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032773#post1032773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you assume ascended aswadim would do anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, replace Aswadim with Bodhisattvas or Examplars for example, who absolutely do have reason to care about their lesser archmage brothers.<br /> <br /> About the remains of the text: Imperial Rites completely rewrite history. The Imperial Rite of Aswadim wouldn't just destroy Earth - it would unmake it's history <i>entirely</i>, as if it have never existed. You can't go back to Fall and unmake it, because Fall never happened in the current Tellurian history at all - only bits and pieces of previous timelines remain. You may try to write Atlantis in history again, but that would anger Exarchs about just as much as destroying the universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:14:23-08:00","id":1032781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032747#post1032747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting part, because it seems that some Ascensions are more likely to permanently affect Tellurian than the others. For example (from now on, these are speculations on material in Imperial Mysteries), Ascension of Hyperion &quot;merely&quot; created the most popular and influential religion ever, and Ascension of Corpus Author seems to have &quot;locked&quot; Mysterium in place, but none of these are as permanent as scale of permanent changes you described.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you think about it, the Fall of the Time Before was 'just' the mass Ascension of an indefinite but finite number of Atlantean mages, and the rise of the Gauntlet was 'just' the death of the most prominent Pangean god, yet they had much more dramatic and lasting effects on the universe than 'ordinary' Ascensions such as the ones of Merlin or the Corpus Author. However, it seems at first glance these other Ascended used much less dramatic Imperium Rites than destroying an advanced magical civilization, physically entering the Supernal by artificial means, kicking out a whole slew of old Supernal gods, and breaking open the Abyss. Or for that matter, causing Pangea to collapse into the Gauntlet. However, an argument might be done in the Exarchs' case their physically breaking in the Supernal instead of going through the 'natural' ways of Ascension was much more damaging to the Universe than it would have otherwise been (e.g. the erasure of Irem wasn't so bad in comparison). I've always had my serious doubts the Fall of Atlantis was enough on a cosmic scale to bring a previously entirely non-existent Abyss into being, unless we assume the Abyss was created because it became the recipient for all the parts of the Tellurian whose truth-symbols the victorious Exarchs cut off from the Supernal into non-existence in order to make room for themselves and cast off the old Supernal Gods. And the death of Father Wolf seems your vanilla Titanomachy event, for good and bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:25:50-08:00","id":1032787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032781#post1032781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless we assume the Abyss was created because it became the recipient for all the parts of the Tellurian whose truth-symbols the victorious Exarchs cut off from the Supernal into non-existence in order to make room for themselves and cast off the old Supernal Gods</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcanon, Abyss was always existing, but before Fall of Atlantis it simply wasn't that agressive and wide. It was simply a place where Paradoxes went from forming Supernal Realms. Fall of Atlantis kicked everything Exarchs didn't liked into the Abyss and they significantly increased it's importance in the new Tellurian by placing it between Supernal and Fallen. In one my game, mages are even found piece of True Atlantis (or one of True Atlantises - it's hard to say) in the Abyss to found out what most of their presumptions about it were wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:40:28-08:00","id":1032799,"title":"","content":"If the Aswadim succeeds in destroying existence, then....existence is destroyed. Everything is the contradictary all-being-all-not-being of the Abyss. You don't have a game until something emerges from the chaos, assuming something <i>can</i> emerge out of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> However, the Pax exists for reasons such as this, and something of that scale is going to get the other Archmages beating down the asshole trying to do it before the rest of reality catches on and kicks <i>all of their asses.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:51:39-08:00","id":1032801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032799#post1032799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the Pax exists for reasons such as this</div> </div> </div> </div>It most explicitly does not.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Pax Arcanum does not apply to Imperium. The Pax exists to prevent archmasters from shattering the Tellurian in open war, beyond the ability of any Seeker to guide through Imperium. Archmages justify this exception by noting that Imperial Practices change how the Phenomenal World manifests,but only Imperium truly changes the basic nature of things. \u201cUnenlightened\u201d individuals may see little difference between things like wiping out a nation and causing it to never exist, but that thin difference is enough for a Seeker to justify Imperium Rites for the sake of her scension. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:54:09-08:00","id":1032802,"title":"","content":"The Pax is an understanding that can end if its adherents are pushed far enough, not a magical rule that prevents intervention. Completely and utterly nullifying the goals of any other archmage with interests in the Fallen World is not something the other Seekers are just going to sit back and allow to happen. Nuclear states don't necessarily want to use their arsenals, but it's not like their hands are helplessly tied if they're pushed too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:55:56-08:00","id":1032806,"title":"","content":"That &quot;Shattering the Tellurian&quot; is the important bit. The Pax is fundamentally focused on keeping an existence around for archmages to exert their will on. THe usual context is archmages fighting each other over their respective visions and causing collateral damage to reality, hence the stuff about Imperium, but if someone is explicitly doing something that will shatter everything, it's well within the pact of &quot;keep the sandbox&quot; to beat the shit out of the Aswadim.<br /> <br /> As has been pointed out, The Pax is not a hard set law-it's more or less an agreement to play nice to keep the sandbox existent. It's flexible as fucking hell, because anything beyond that is impossible to enforce among the celestial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:01:47-08:00","id":1032808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032802#post1032802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pax is an understanding that can end if its adherents are pushed far enough, not a magical rule that prevents intervention. Completely and utterly nullifying the goals of any other archmage with interests in the Fallen World is not something the other Seekers are just going to sit back and allow to happen. Nuclear states don't necessarily want to use their arsenals, but it's not like their hands are helplessly tied if they're pushed too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what Ascension War about, and my question is what happens <i>after somebody wins</i> - unlikely, rare, but not impossible event. If you dislike my example with destroying the Earth - take an Supreme Celestial Omen for an example: &quot;Create a new Celestial Ladder&quot;. What happens after one has been built? It is stays forever? Is it going to be destroyed and how does that affect Ascended Seeker who built it? Please don't give me an answer &quot;That's not going to happen&quot;, because this isn't answer to the question I asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032806#post1032806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That &quot;Shattering the Tellurian&quot; is the important bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost every Omen above Legendary is introducing such massive change what it is on par with shattering the Tellurian. Again - the question isn't &quot;Is it likely what somebody could introduce such massive change and get away with it?&quot;. The question is &quot;What happens after someone does it and Ascend?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:10:03-08:00","id":1032815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032808#post1032808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost every Omen above Legendary is introducing such massive change what it is on par with shattering the Tellurian. Again - the question isn't &quot;Is it likely what somebody could introduce such massive change and get away with it?&quot;. The question is &quot;What happens after someone does it and Ascend?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave you the answer for the example you gave.<br /> <br /> These other examples still have a reality to play around with, and archmasters who 'lost' now have to contend with a Tellurian that has established an Ascended's vision as The Way Things Are. It's a setback, because they basically have an immovable object in the way of their own visions of reality, but you don't get to be an archmage by giving up because someone put a mountain in your way.<br /> <br /> The example you gave is an explicit &quot;We all lose&quot; scenario, which is why people are pointing out the asskicking that would happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:15:31-08:00","id":1032821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032815#post1032815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These other examples still have a reality to play around with, and archmasters who 'lost' now have to contend with a Tellurian that has established an Ascended's vision as The Way Things Are. It's a setback, because they basically have an immovable object in the way of their own visions of reality</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the part that interests me. How much of an immovable object it is? Is it possible to undo Supernal Truth which were introduced by someone Ascending? Can you even do it without de-Ascending somebody? Because it is much more less of an &quot;We all lose&quot; scenario if you can just shrug and re-create Earth history from scratch - even against Supernal truth that Earth, in fact, never existed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:17:01-08:00","id":1032823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032821#post1032821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the part that interests me. How much of an immovable object it is? Is it possible to undo Supernal Truth which were introduced by someone Ascending? Can you even do it without de-Ascending somebody? Because it is much more less of an &quot;We all lose&quot; scenario if you can just shrug and re-create Earth history from scratch - even against Supernal truth that Earth, in fact, never existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how you'll never actually find Atlantis?<br /> <br /> That much of an immovable object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:19:34-08:00","id":1032825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032823#post1032823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how you'll never actually find Atlantis?</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually can, that's Supreme Personal Omen. Or you can re-create it, or make your own, those are God-like Earthly Omens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:20:38-08:00","id":1032826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032825#post1032825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You actually can, that's Supreme Personal Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still by and large sets the standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:24:52-08:00","id":1032831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032826#post1032826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still by and large sets the standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Imperial Rites and Practices <i>can </i>change the results of previous Imperial Rites? Shouldn't be a problem for interested Ascended beings, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:25:48-08:00","id":1032833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032831#post1032831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Imperial Rites and Practices <i>can </i>change the results of previous Imperial Rites? Shouldn't be a problem for interested Ascended beings, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if it's in the books, or just something Dave mentioned, but the Exarchs rewrote Camelot out of reality after Merlin Ascended. <br /> So yeah, it's a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:28:51-08:00","id":1032836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032833#post1032833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it's in the books, or just something Dave mentioned, but the Exarchs rewrote Camelot out of reality after Merlin Ascended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to address the issue, but nothing in the book says that Camelot was a result of Imperial Rite and Merlin's Noumenon, not a big side-project for personal gratification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:30:20-08:00","id":1032838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032836#post1032836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to address the issue, but nothing in the book says that Camelot was a result of Imperial Rite and Merlin's Noumenon, not a big side-project for personal gratification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of what Dave has said on Merlin and Camelot hasn't appeared in the books directly, but it still clearly represents much of what is going on with this entire shenanigan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:31:38-08:00","id":1032839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032836#post1032836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to address the issue, but nothing in the book says that Camelot was a result of Imperial Rite and Merlin's Noumenon, not a big side-project for personal gratification.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40121#post40121\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40121#post40121\"> Camelot? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40121#post40121\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40121#post40121 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm curious with what we have of Camelot. What I gather is that Merlin was an Acanthus Archmaster (probably Silver Ladder) that manipulated destinies and time to create an utopia. Eventually Camelot was erased from time by the Exarchs, but sparked lots of variant stories. But was it really erased? The </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unless you're one of those Death of the Author types, that should satisfy your need for an official answer.<br /> Doesn't mean you can't rule differently if it works for you, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:56:34-08:00","id":1032855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032768#post1032768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Imperial Rite changes entire history retroactively, I really fail to see the difference. Of course they agreed. Their entire history was written in such way that they agreed on &quot;one Order thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But history still points there <i>were </i>before two Orders - till 1200s we have globally both Pancryptias and Keepers of the Word. I think we can assume that till 1300s there are still enclaves of those single Orders, before Mysterium joins unifiys them totally.<br /> <br /> What's more, for your 'magical swapping interpretation of Imperium' it imply that Corpus Author <b>created</b> world in that both of predecessors of Mysterium were made by her Ascension. I.E. You are implying that Author created idea of Gnostikon Darshana. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And by this you are implying that Corpus Author created retroactively Diamond Order (as they ALL strive from uncovering Darshana commodity of mage cults in Alexanderian times) - if Corpus Author created one Darshana idea, she needed to create then others. And by this you are implying that Corpus Author created what mages describe as 'Atlantean society'.<br /> <br /> Basically, going from your point of view, Corpus Author just created Atlantis origins for magic to prove her thesis to join two Orders on Living Magic. Which is terrifying. And just wrong - as Time Before Ruins were all long before life of Corpus Author. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:31:56-08:00","id":1032880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032855#post1032855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your 'magical swapping interpretation of Imperium'</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not my interpretation, it's how Imperium is described in Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once an Omen has been fully Exalted, the desires it symbolizes change the universe. They become Supernal symbols, her imagination shaping the cosmos so that it has always been this way. History, physics, art, culture, Invisible Realms, and even the true nature of Atlantis conform to her vision. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the archmage fi lls every box of his Omen with Exaltation points, the Omen becomes a Supernal Truth. The desires it represents become Supernal Symbols and emanate throughout the Tellurian. If he wished that a god had never existed, it never did. If he desired an ancient cult that prophesied his coming as the Hieromagus, it has always existed, waiting for him to redeem the Awakened. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032855#post1032855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, going from your point of view, Corpus Author just created Atlantis origins for magic to prove her thesis to join two Orders on Living Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032855#post1032855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time Before Ruins were all long before life of Corpus Author</div> </div> </div> </div>...yes? That's the Imperial Rites - massive rewrite of history to match your image of history of cosmos. Including history, physics, mystical societies, conspiracies, Diamond Orders and yes, &quot;true&quot; nature of Atlantis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:39:03-08:00","id":1033229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032880#post1032880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...yes? That's the Imperial Rites - massive rewrite of history to match your image of history of cosmos. Including history, physics, mystical societies, conspiracies, Diamond Orders and yes, &quot;true&quot; nature of Atlantis.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it cannot be made for Atlantis idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then whole greatest Mystery of setting lose <i>any </i>sense. It would be just 'Corpus Author liked Atlantis so much, we all need to love it now'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For me, Author, by her Ascension, show that 'she was right' not that 'she made world to adhere to her thesis'. Basically, <u>she did not</u> made proper Imperial Rites, only 'went to Heavens', as she become one with things she <b>uncovered</b> were Truth, <i>not</i> making the Truth herself. Hint: She is clearly stated in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> as <i>only</i> Gnosis 9 Archmage, so her Ascension can be 'not full'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2017, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:48:23-08:00","id":1033246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033229#post1033229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it cannot be made for Atlantis idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then whole greatest Mystery of setting lose <i>any </i>sense.(</div> </div> </div> </div>It never had any sense. Original Atlantis is <i>gone</i>. Only Exarchs and Oracles can have any memory about true Atlantis, and they are not sharing. In fact, it is stated:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If archmage wants to impose a truth about nature of Atlantis, he might have to seek out and destroy the contradictory evidence. </div> </div> </div>So truth about Atlanits may have been rewritten so many time that by the time Author Ascended, she wasn't changing &quot;original&quot; Atlantis, she was changing the idea for Atlantis of previous archmaster who cared enough about it to include it in the Noumenon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033229#post1033229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Author, by her Ascension, show that 'she was right' not that 'she made world to adhere to her thesis'. Basically, <u>she did not</u> made proper Imperial Rites, only 'went to Heavens', as she become one with things she <b>uncovered</b> were Truth, <i>not</i> making the Truth herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are grasping at the straws now. Imperial Rites are most clearly stated to overwriting the Truth itself. Her &quot;being right&quot; have no meaning whatsoever if actual Truth can be rewritten by any next Archmage, or Ascended Being (like Exarchs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033229#post1033229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hint: She is clearly stated in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> as <i>only</i> Gnosis 9 Archmage, so her Ascension can be 'not full'.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, she is clearly stated to have Ascended, listed among Ascended archmages and indirectly said to not be an archmage: &quot;she now serves as inspiration and mentor to Seekers (other archmages) <b>one more step removed up the ladder</b>&quot;. Following stats are meant for her avatar-Ochemata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:53:49-08:00","id":1033288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033229#post1033229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hint: She is clearly stated in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> as <i>only</i> Gnosis 9 Archmage, so her Ascension can be 'not full'</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosis 10 isn't a prerequisite for Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:44:55-08:00","id":1033320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1032821#post1032821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the part that interests me. How much of an immovable object it is? Is it possible to undo Supernal Truth which were introduced by someone Ascending? Can you even do it without de-Ascending somebody? Because it is much more less of an &quot;We all lose&quot; scenario if you can just shrug and re-create Earth history from scratch - even against Supernal truth that Earth, in fact, never existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where it gets funny: Supernal Truths <i>can</i> be undone, but it isn't guaranteed. You can do it without de-Ascending people, too, though de-Ascending people is also possible through the right actions as well.<br /> <br /> The trouble is that such Imperium Rites require a kind of shadow play; a symbolic act or acts that may or may not be possible. While Supernal beings are a part of the Godhead and, thus, can probably accomplish most miracles that could characterize a Lesser Omen with relatively little difficulty, even for them, the highest miracles will be difficult and every failure pushes the possibility out of reach. A doomsday scenario may even outright destroy the possibilities of symbolic acts necessary to undo the harm, or may make the acts themselves so risky and difficult that even success could eternally transmute and diminish a Supernal being.<br /> <br /> For that reason, a doomsday scenario might really not be the awful conclusion it appears to be but any hope or certainty that what follows is &quot;As if it were just a bad dream&quot; is tentative at best.<br /> <br /> Imperium is true divine power to rewrite the universe according to one's will, but that power is a possibility, not a promise. In other words, everyone has a good reason to make sure R.E.M. is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:46:20-08:00","id":1033460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033246#post1033246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never had any sense. Original Atlantis is <i>gone</i>. Only Exarchs and Oracles can have any memory about true Atlantis, and they are not sharing. In fact, it is stated:<br /> <br /> So truth about Atlanits may have been rewritten so many time that by the time Author Ascended, she wasn't changing &quot;original&quot; Atlantis, she was changing the idea for Atlantis of previous archmaster who cared enough about it to include it in the Noumenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, here is thing - Atlantis <i>needed </i>to exist before Corpus Author. as people before here were trying to recreate it in Fallen World. And Exarchs destroyed those attempts every time. So Supernal Tyrants must BEFORE Corpus Author <b>really</b> disliked 'Atlantis' ideas.<br /> <br /> For example Merlin is officially stated as Silver Ladder Acanthus Archmage that wanted to create Atlantis-like kingdom of Camelot - only Exarchs become jealous, and twisted Fate magic he build kingdom upon, creating Mordred, Kingslayer Son of Arthur. There are also other 'Atlantis attempts' in canon, like Minoan Atlantis - see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">Ancient Era section of Awakened Timeline</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033246#post1033246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are grasping at the straws now. Imperial Rites are most clearly stated to overwriting the Truth itself. Her &quot;being right&quot; have no meaning whatsoever if actual Truth can be rewritten by any next Archmage, or Ascended Being (like Exarchs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Uff, so she really <i>did nothing</i>, as some other Ascended Being return everything to enter state, before her Imperial Rite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:55:01-08:00","id":1033467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033460#post1033460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example Merlin is officially stated as Silver Ladder Acanthus Archmage that wanted to create Atlantis-like kingdom of Camelot - only Exarchs become jealous, and twisted Fate magic he build kingdom upon, creating Mordred, Kingslayer Son of Arthur.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Merlin</i> orchestrated the downfall of Camelot. His Noumenon concerned the link between the fates of a country and its king.<br /> <br /> The Prophet in particular Was Not Happy About This, because it's pretty much a direct thumb in Her eye, but that led to the place being erased from history, not made to fall like it already had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:19:43-08:00","id":1033484,"title":"","content":"I dig out Words of God on the topic of Merlin ( so 'almost' canon ) / that is planned to be added in Britain Dark Ages Dark Era, if ever written. / <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952388#post952388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arthurian World did exist (in some form, it was probably closer to earlier Dark Ages, Arthur laughing as he wrestles bears and smites men versions than after it got lancelotted and romantic fantasied) sometime in post-Roman Britain. It was the pet project of a welsh Silver Ladder Acanthus (and either the founder of or an early member of the Walkers in Mists Legacy) with the Shadow Name of Myrddin (or, in English, Merlin). He achieved archmastery, and his Noumenon, the great act of magic that made him Ascend, was to manipulate Fate to great and then doom the society he built, marking the Symbolism of Arcadia forever. Among the side effects was turning the astral anthropomorphism of Fate into Mordred.<br /> <br /> Then the Arcadian Exarchs deleted the whole thing from the timeline, and history became as we know it. Myrddin, safely Ascended as the very symbol of a cunning bastard, gave no shits.<br /> <br /> Tldr - it is a longstanding setting element of Mage, since Tome of the Watchtowers nearly ten years ago, that Merlin was a real mage, that the crystal cave was what he *wanted* (his ascension) and the fall of Camelot was entirely deliberate on his part. It predates Changeling as a gameline.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't set a Dark Era during it, anyway. The Anarchy era mentioned above would draw inspiration from things like Cadfael and the Pillars of the Earth, and be based on the last major conflict between the two Orders that would later merge to become the Mysterium. In a Britain falling apart, should mages stay hidden or attempt to guide Sleepers? Monastic Diamond mages fighting a war of ideals in the midst of a civil war.<br /> <br /> It's just that the mages of the setting would use their own context for &quot;Atlantean&quot; things, and be unable to tell them apart from the abandoned scaffolding of Myrddin's scheming. What if the civil war wakes the red and white dragons? What do the nearly-vanished children of Gog and Magog make of the chaos in the mortal realm?<br /> <br /> And does Myrddin, archetypal Jerkass Acanthus, see what's happening from the Supernal and decide to get involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:29:00-08:00","id":1033490,"title":"","content":"So you're saying, &quot;Oops, you're right Satchel.&quot; ...? Because that basically just proved his point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:35:40-08:00","id":1033500,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I just admit to my mistake - and yes, Setchel is right here. And now I <i>hate</i> Merlin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:38:49-08:00","id":1033504,"title":"","content":"Well, he's a real bastard, but bright side he did one over on the Prophet. Exarchs can suck it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T01:44:19-08:00","id":1033921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033460#post1033460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, here is thing - Atlantis <i>needed </i>to exist before Corpus Author. as people before here were trying to recreate it in Fallen World. And Exarchs destroyed those attempts every time. So Supernal Tyrants must BEFORE Corpus Author <b>really</b> disliked 'Atlantis' ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it did, but it by no means was original Atlantis - that one was wiped off by Exarchs long time ago and maybe supplanted by some other Ascended beign as part of it's Imperial Rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033460#post1033460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uff, so she really <i>did nothing</i>, as some other Ascended Being return everything to enter state, before her Imperial Rite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>She wouldn't have Ascended, if they did. Exaltation of all your Imperial Rites is required for Ascension by Imperium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T04:35:06-08:00","id":1033955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033921#post1033921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She wouldn't have Ascended, if they did. Exaltation of all your Imperial Rites is required for Ascension by Imperium.</div> </div> </div> </div>She could Asended by showing 'your two Orders can be one in reality' - and that part become Truth. BUT rest of it's implications - the changing whole Atlantis hailing from Corpus Author - could be erased by other Ascend beings - just like Exarchs wiped out Camelot for Merlin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T05:50:51-08:00","id":1033970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033921#post1033921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it did, but it by no means was original Atlantis - that one was wiped off by Exarchs long time ago and maybe supplanted by some other Ascended beign as part of it's Imperial Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that assumption on? It might be right, but a common Awakened belief is that Atlantis Ascended as much as the Exarchs did; that the Awakened City itself is now a Supernal ideal. Given that Ruins of the Time Before exist in prehistory, all of which are remnants of a city full of magic centred on Supernal Verges, the idea isn't without merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:15:52-08:00","id":1034613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1033970#post1033970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you basing that assumption on?</div> </div> </div> </div>On history of Atlantis in 1e core book and fact that none of Atlantean ruins seem to share an common origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:53:03-08:00","id":1034633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1034613#post1034613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On history of Atlantis in 1e core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always A LEGEND about Altantis - typical story Mentor can told to his Aprentice, just to show pices of Truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1034613#post1034613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fact that none of Atlantean ruins seem to share an common origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were many 'Atlantean' civilizations in our universe - but in previous version(s) of cosmos there was<i> original</i> ( the most first one ) Atlantis that become blueprint for any 'magical civilization'. And from it's Rise and Fall, every other magical culture has quasi-Oracle and quasi-Exarchs beings that lead to various Falls of them - leading to different Ruins of Time Before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:53:04-08:00","id":1034632,"title":"","content":"Double Post, sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:40:18-08:00","id":1034663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1034613#post1034613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On history of Atlantis in 1e core book and fact that none of Atlantean ruins seem to share an common origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lack of unifying appearance or even history is not a problem for Supernal beings. The Exarchs have many different forms, varying with time, space, and culture; their ochema, even, may bare no resemblance to one another. Supernal things are a Platonic Ideal, and the physical form that ideal takes in the Fallen World is an expression; a facet of a purer truth as perceived by the circumstances by which it enters.<br /> <br /> Ruins of the Time Before are Supernal in origin - centred and dependent as they are upon Supernal Verges. That means that they could easily represent the Supernal ideal of Atlantis without needing to share any unifying features save the raw concept behind them: A magical civilization, once arisen, now in ruins.<br /> <br /> Whether this is correct or not is a matter of debate, but it fits the evidence just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:55:44-08:00","id":1034719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences#post1032595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so here is my question. Let's assume we have Aswadim (for example, Theumiel from Imperial Mysteries), who have accepted Supreme Earthly Omen - to destroy all Earth by flooding in the Abyss. <i>The Pax Arcanum does not apply to Imperium</i>, so technically Exarchs can't just punch him in the face outright without other Ascended Aswadim to retaliate (let's assume they care enough about our Aswadim for some reason). Our Aswadim prepares his Rites, create doomsday cults and prophecies, create his Anti-Messiah, Seals his Omens, then Exalts them and poof! He is Descended and Earth is destroyed.<br /> What happens next? As I understand, destruction of Earth is Supernal Truth on some level now - perfect and unassailable. Do Exarchs re-create world from the scratch? Can they do it without destroying Supernal Truth about destruction of Earth? Is changes brought by Ascension are immutable and perfect, or they are just as any other Supernal Truth - malleable by sufficiently strong power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Camalot was erased from history and became a tale with supernatural side effects/trace evidence, it is likely the same would or has happen to the story you just described. perhaps biblical Revelations, HP Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos events, I am Legend, and a dozen other such &quot;ends of the world&quot; have actually happened and there are artifacts to find from those events, but they were taken out of the main timeline. Perhaps that these things actually happened before they were edited out is why the fiction and stories are so strong in the collective zeitgeist and in game Astral realms.<br /> <br /> Future, present, or past tenses are really meaningless when it comes to viewing reality and time as an artificial constructs. This fits how the world has evidence to things that never were are just hanging out in some places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-19-2017, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:48:30-08:00","id":1034907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032595-imperium-rites-ascension-and-it-s-consequences?p=1034633#post1034633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were many 'Atlantean' civilizations in our universe - but in previous version(s) of cosmos there was<i> original</i> ( the most first one ) Atlantis that become blueprint for any 'magical civilization'. And from it's Rise and Fall, every other magical culture has quasi-Oracle and quasi-Exarchs beings that lead to various Falls of them - leading to different Ruins of Time Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I am not doubting that. All I say is that &quot;original&quot; Atlantis didn't exist in any current timeline. It doesn't matter if it's became an Supernal Truth - there never was an Awakened City in current timeline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:06:32-08:00","id":1034917,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's what you're saying? Yeah, that isn't disputed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}